   "id": 646694,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"4\" type=\"1\">\n    <li>What are the equations of the two lines shown?<br><img alt=\"This graph shows two lines on an x, y coordinate plane. The \\(x\\)-axis runs from negative 4 to 6. The \\(y\\)-axis runs from negative 3 to 8.  The first line has the equation y = -3 times x divided by 2 plus 1.  The second line has the equation y = -3 times x divided by 2 plus 7.  The lines do not cross.\" src=\"exercises/media/da74fbd18c52ecd2.jpg\" width=\"400\">       <p> <strong>Select two </strong>that apply:</p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <ol start=\"1\" type=\"a\">\n    <li><span data-math=\"y=x+4\">y=x+4</span></li>\n    <li><span data-math=\"y=x-4\">y=x-4</span></li>\n    <li><span data-math=\"y=-\\frac32x+1\">y=-\\frac32x+1</span></li>\n    <li><span data-math=\"y=\\frac32x-7\">y=\\frac32x-7</span></li>\n    <li><span data-math=\"y=\\frac32x+1\">y=\\frac32x+1</span></li>\n    <li><span data-math=\"y=-\\frac32x+7\">y=-\\frac32x+7</span></li>\n  </ol>",
